{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "First words",
  "goal": "Greet people, say yes and no, thank, apologise and choose the right 'you' for the person in front of you.",
  "intro": "Malayalis are warm but not effusive with words: a smile, a nod and a sideways head tilt often do the work of 'hello' and 'thanks'. Still, a handful of words will carry you a long way.\n\nNotice that Malayalam has **two different 'no's**: അല്ല *alla* ('it is not [that]') and ഇല്ല *illa* ('there isn't / didn't / doesn't'). We'll meet them properly in unit 2, but start noticing them now.",
  "vocab": [
